"""Stored-state checks for the OpenWireshark workflow tasks.

OpenWireshark keeps its whole workspace in the browser Local Storage document
``openwireshark.state.v1``: the selected profile, the applied display filter,
the selected packet, the packet-byte view, the active statistics view, the
packet colouring flag and the zoom level.  A task ends with a specific
combination of those settings, so the terminal document is the durable outcome
this module judges.

The document is read through the runtime controller; when no controller is
present the Local Storage directory is read in-process.  The terminal settings
declared by the task parameters are used when present, and otherwise the
terminal settings named by the task instruction are used.
"""

